Here's the exact click-path for each screenshot.

Setup (one time)
1. Grafana password:


cat ~/platform-infrastructure/envs/state/grafana-admin-password.txt
2. Import the dashboard — open http://localhost:9093/dashboard/import

log in: user admin, the password above
click Upload dashboard JSON file → pick ~/ai-notification-system/loadtest/grafana-phaseF.json
Prometheus datasource dropdown → select Prometheus
click Import
you land on the dashboard. Its permanent URL is http://localhost:9093/d/phase-f-loadtest
top-right: set range to Last 15 minutes, refresh to 5s
Run the load
Terminal 1 — CPU numbers:


export KUBECONFIG=~/platform-infrastructure/envs/state/kubeconfig-ai-notification-floci
while :; do clear; date +%T; kubectl top pods -n ai-notification --sort-by=cpu; sleep 2; done
Terminal 2 — 3-minute overload:


cd ~/ai-notification-system && export PATH="$HOME/bin:$HOME/.docker/bin:$PATH"
caffeinate -i k6 run -e RATE=12 -e DURATION=3m loadtest/hold.js
Wait ~60 seconds (let the graphs fill), then take the shots below. You have ~2 min.

Screenshots
In Grafana (http://localhost:9093/d/phase-f-loadtest) — to isolate one panel: hover it, press v (fullscreen), screenshot, press Esc.

#	Panel title on the dashboard	What it should show
1	Pod CPU (cores) vs the 250m limit ← the bottleneck	event-service + api-gateway lines flat on the red 0.25 line
2	CPU throttling ratio	those two pods jumping to 0.5–0.9
3	POST /events — latency percentiles (red = 300ms SLO)	p95/p99 lifting off the red line to multiple seconds
4	POST /events — request rate by status_code	a 504 band appearing on top of the 201 band
5	RabbitMQ — backlog, unacked, publish rate...	"messages ready (backlog)" ramping up
6	Whole dashboard (no fullscreen)	one wide shot of everything degrading together
In Prometheus (optional, for a raw-query shot) — open http://localhost:9094/graph

paste in the query box: sum by (pod) (rate(container_cpu_cfs_throttled_periods_total{namespace="ai-notification"}[1m])) / sum by (pod) (rate(container_cpu_cfs_periods_total{namespace="ai-notification"}[1m]))
click Graph tab → Execute → screenshot (#7)
In Jaeger — open http://localhost:9095/search

Service → api-gateway
Operation → POST /events
Min Duration → type 3s
Lookback → Last Hour
Limit Results → 20
click Find Traces
